From b1bc3dc36a905a6dc0373c4fed0a12aab3e73991
Subject: Expose participant_identity on RoomEvent::DataReceived
Origin: https://github.com/robtfm/client-sdk-rust/commit/b1bc3dc36a905a6dc0373c4fed0a12aab3e73991
Date: 2026-10-25T12:02:10+00:00

handle_data receives the sender identity stamped on the packet by the
server but drops it when the participant lookup misses, so data from a
participant the room has not been told about yet reaches the
application with no way to attribute it. That happens for the first
packets of every joiner: the server announces a participant to its
peers only once it is active, while its data channel is already open.

Pass the identity through on the event, mirroring
livekit/client-sdk-js#2092, so callers can attribute or buffer such
data. The FFI's DataPacketReceived.participant_identity is filled from
it in that case instead of being left empty.
---
diff --git a/livekit/src/room/mod.rs b/livekit/src/room/mod.rs
index 172cf5a5ef0b588798453c75b45903929948bf93..81da806ad04337a640d6ef21c8a4be27fb0ebde3 100644
--- a/livekit/src/room/mod.rs
+++ b/livekit/src/room/mod.rs
@@ -209,6 +209,7 @@ pub enum RoomEvent {
         topic: Option<String>,
         kind: DataPacketKind,
         participant: Option<RemoteParticipant>,
+        participant_identity: Option<ParticipantIdentity>,
     },
     TranscriptionReceived {
         participant: Option<Participant>,
@@ -1880,6 +1881,7 @@ impl RoomSession {
             topic,
             kind,
             participant,
+            participant_identity,
         });
     }
 
